.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
CAD/old
CAD
# Top-level docs/ only. Software/UTM_PyQt6/docs/ is the app's own reference material and IS
# tracked - a bare "docs/" matched it too, so every new file there was silently untracked
# (STALL_GUARD.md sat unpublished while commits pointed readers at it).
/docs/
!Software/UTM_PyQt6/docs/

Software/data
Software/dataCiP
TestingMachine
guides/QUICKSTART.qmd

Software/QT_test/main.py
Software/QT_test/test.ui
D32_Firmware/.vscode/extensions.json
Software/UTM_PyQt6/__pycache__/
.claude/settings.local.json

# PyInstaller build artifacts
Software/UTM_PyQt6/build/
Software/UTM_PyQt6/dist/
Software/UTM_PyQt6/*.spec

# Test data files
*.csv
# ...and the .orig backups left by header rewrites, which are the same data
*.csv.orig

# Claude Code / AI documentation (local only)
CLAUDE.md
APP_DESCRIPTION.qmd
Software/UTM_PyQt6/DEPLOYMENT.md
PROJECT_STATUS.md

Software/testData/
Software/data*

# Large binaries / installers
*.exe

# Generated per-test reports (local artifacts, like the CSVs)
Software/UTM_PyQt6/reports/

# User-saved test settings ("Settings" dropdown — local per machine; Default is auto-created)
Software/UTM_PyQt6/recipes/

# Python bytecode (any location)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- UTM_PyQt6 scratch/rig artifacts (added 2026-08-09) -----------------------
# Debug frames regenerated by the camera/DIC test scripts. Targeted patterns, NOT
# a blanket *.png, so the tracked ui_help/ diagrams and the deck plots stay in git.
Software/UTM_PyQt6/binary_*.png
Software/UTM_PyQt6/check_blobs.png
Software/UTM_PyQt6/live_frame.png
Software/UTM_PyQt6/test_*.png
Software/UTM_PyQt6/utm_annotated.png

# Rig test-data folders (the CSVs are already covered by *.csv above, but these
# also hold session plots/photos)
Software/UTM_PyQt6/8.6.3/
Software/UTM_PyQt6/8.7/
Software/UTM_PyQt6/8.6.20 - Tensile test to Failure/

# Session video / phone photos
*.mp4
Software/UTM_PyQt6/*.jpg

# DIC frame capture / video recording output (huge: ~1.9 GB per minute of PNGs)
# The rule under this comment was EMPTY: it used to be covered by Software/UTM_PyQt6/output/,
# and the capture folders now sit beside the CSVs under "Test data/". Matched by SHAPE
# rather than by location so the next reorganisation cannot silently lose it again.
# S26 alone is 1.7 GB of stills + 266 MB of video.
**/frames*/
*.avi
*.mkv
*.tif
*.tiff

# Session pack for the MOT extensometer visit. Documents are copies (the originals are
# tracked or generated); the operator drops multi-GB videos in here before travelling, which
# must never reach git.
Validation docs/

# PowerPoint slide renders used only to proof-read the deck
documentation/deck_png_tpu/

# Diagnostic images written by the scripts in Software/UTM_PyQt6/tools and /tests


# Everything the app and its tools write: captures, diagnostics, setup and ROI output
Software/UTM_PyQt6/output/
# Slide renders used only to proof-read a deck
documentation/deck_png_*/

# Fallback deck the generators write when the real .pptx is open in PowerPoint. It is a
# STALE duplicate the moment the lock clears and the real file is rebuilt, so it must never
# be committed alongside it.
documentation/decks/*_updated.pptx
# Throwaway copies made to export slide PNGs — PowerPoint keeps a handle on them, so the
# rm after an export often loses the race and they turn up staged.
documentation/decks/_*.pptx

# built release archives
deploy/dist/

# Basler USB3 Vision driver: PUBLISHED 2026-08-30 by decision of the project owner, who reads
# Basler's EULA as covering this academic use - the students use Basler cameras and therefore
# need the Basler driver. deploy/driver/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
